-- title:
--   Ordinarity at p transports along a factorisation of Hecke–Galois data
-- statement:
--   Fix a level $N \ge 1$ and a finite set $S$ of natural numbers, and let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology) with a ring homomorphism $\theta$ from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-$2$ cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$, and the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$ — to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$. Let $T_0$ and $T$ be Noetherian local $\mathcal{O}$-algebras, complete for their maximal-ideal topologies, with local structure maps, finite and free as $\mathcal{O}$-modules, and let $H_0$, $H$ be Hecke–Galois representation data of type $(N, S, \mathcal{O}, \theta)$ over $T_0$ and over $T$: each consists of a Hecke homomorphism $\pi$ reducing to $\theta$, with $\mathcal{O}$-algebra generated by its image, a lifting property for $\mathcal{O}$-valued characters reducing to $\theta$, surjectivity of $\mathcal{O}$ onto the residue field, and a rank-$2$ adically continuous Galois representation $\rho$ whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials at good $\ell$ are $X^2 - \pi(T_\ell)X + \ell$ and whose residual representation is absolutely irreducible. Let $\varphi : T_0 \to T$ be a local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism with $\varphi(H_0.\pi(t)) = H.\pi(t)$ for all $t$, and suppose $H_0.\rho$ is ordinary at a natural number $p$, meaning that for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $P$ there is a $T_0$-submodule $L$ of the representation space spanned by the first member of some basis indexed by `Fin 2`, stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$, and such that every element of the inertia subgroup of $P$ acts trivially modulo $L$. Then there exists a Hecke–Galois representation datum $H'$ of the same type over $T$ with $H'.\pi = H.\pi$ and $H'.\rho$ ordinary at $p$.
--
--   This is the transport of the ordinarity condition along a map of Hecke–Galois data: a datum over $T$ whose Hecke homomorphism is the given one can be chosen so that its Galois representation is ordinary at $p$, provided the datum over $T_0$ through which the Hecke homomorphism factors is. It is used in the variant where ordinarity is required at all primes dividing a given number, as part of the modularity-lifting input.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_HeckeGaloisRepDatum_exists_pi_eq_and_isOrdinaryAt_of_comp_pi_eq.lean

